Revision history for Game-Reversi

0.04    2026-10-13
	- Add options, the fields a launcher offers before a game
	- The keys, the screen and the cursor steering are Game::Terminal::Kit's
	- Requires perl 5.14
	- The picker redraws in place, and shift-tab walks the squares backwards
	- Fix: after t the square you type was not echoed
	- to_text and from_text carry the variant, the first colour, the starting board, the seed, and a resignation, timeout or abandonment
	- Add u and r, and typed undo and redo, to take a turn back and play it again; start plays a game it is given

0.03    2026-10-11
	- Add Game::Reversi::Terminal->run(@argv), which returns the exit status

0.02    2026-10-10
	- Fix: Terminal.pm POD declares =encoding utf8, so t/pod.t passes.
	- Fix: --level took any number. The variant was brought into BUILD when
	  that bug was found; the level was left in the Bot, three calls deeper,
	  and died with a file and a line at exit 25.
	- Point at the move you mean: the arrow keys walk the squares marked *
	  and the line under the board says what the move would turn and what
	  the score would become.
	- The square the last move went on is bracketed and the discs it turned
	  are drawn ringed, so what just happened is readable with --ascii and
	  with colour off.
	- Fix: a refusal or a redrawn board landed on the prompt's own line off
	  a terminal.

0.01    2026-09-15
	First version
